<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Functions on Alfero Chingono</title><link>https://www.chingono.com/tags/functions/</link><description>Recent content in Functions on Alfero Chingono</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Sun, 05 Apr 2026 15:34:04 -0400</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.chingono.com/tags/functions/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Adding Azure Functions Support to a Devcontainer</title><link>https://www.chingono.com/blog/2022/09/23/adding-azure-functions-support-devcontainer/</link><pubDate>Fri, 23 Sep 2022 15:58:13 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.chingono.com/blog/2022/09/23/adding-azure-functions-support-devcontainer/</guid><description>&lt;img src="https://www.chingono.com/blog/2022/09/23/adding-azure-functions-support-devcontainer/cover.png" alt="Featured image of post Adding Azure Functions Support to a Devcontainer" /&gt;&lt;h1 id="adding-azure-functions-support-to-a-devcontainer"&gt;Adding Azure Functions Support to a Devcontainer
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;I already had a dev container set up and needed to add Azure Functions Core Tools to it. This is the approach that finally worked for me.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="the-challenge"&gt;The Challenge
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I needed to add support for &lt;a class="link" href="https://azure.microsoft.com/products/functions/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
&gt;Azure Functions&lt;/a&gt; to my existing &lt;a class="link" href="https://learn.microsoft.com/training/modules/use-docker-container-dev-env-vs-code/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
&gt;Dev Container&lt;/a&gt;. I tried a few approaches and hit errors along the way. After some digging through the docs and a bit of trial and error, I landed on a version that rebuilt cleanly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="the-solution"&gt;The Solution
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;To begin, I attempted to add the following lines to my &lt;code&gt;Dockerfile&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That version failed when I rebuilt the container. After searching around and comparing a few examples, I landed on this &lt;code&gt;RUN&lt;/code&gt; command:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;4
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;5
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;6
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-Dockerfile" data-lang="Dockerfile"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;RUN&lt;/span&gt; curl https://packages.microsoft.com/keys/microsoft.asc &lt;span class="p"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; gpg --dearmor &amp;gt; microsoft.gpg &lt;span class="se"&gt;\
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; sudo mv microsoft.gpg /etc/apt/trusted.gpg.d/microsoft.gpg &lt;span class="se"&gt;\
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; apt-get update &lt;span class="se"&gt;\
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; sudo sh -c &lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;echo &amp;#34;deb [arch=amd64] https://packages.microsoft.com/debian/$(lsb_release -rs | cut -d&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39; -f 1)/prod $(lsb_release -cs) main&amp;#34; &amp;gt; /etc/apt/sources.list.d/dotnetdev.list&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="se"&gt;\
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; sudo apt-get update &lt;span class="se"&gt;\
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; apt-get -y install azure-functions-core-tools-4&lt;span class="err"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;This successfully rebuilt the container image and had the &lt;a class="link" href="https://github.com/Azure/azure-functions-core-tools" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
&gt;Azure Functions Core Tools&lt;/a&gt; installed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Next, I added the following extensions to the &lt;code&gt;devcontainer.json&lt;/code&gt; file:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;4
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;5
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;6
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-json" data-lang="json"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;extensions&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;ms-azuretools.vscode-azurefunctions&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;ms-vscode.azure-account&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;ms-azuretools.vscode-azureresourcegroups&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;azurite.azurite&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;With that in place, I had a working dev container with Azure Functions Core Tools and the Visual Studio Code extensions I needed.&lt;/p&gt;
